{#
    Shared subtitle-language chip strip (Bazarr visual & detail pass, Task 1).
    One chip per language: green for a language that already has subtitles,
    red for one still missing. Small superscript markers flag hearing-impaired
    (HI) and forced tracks. Consumed server-side by Tasks 4/7; a later JS task
    mirrors this exact markup to inject chips client-side, so the class list
    here (`badge poster-chip is-success` / `badge poster-chip is-danger`) must
    stay stable — don't rename or reorder without updating that JS too.

    Deliberately NOT bg-success-lt/bg-danger-lt: those Tabler classes set
    background-color with !important and resolve to a translucent tint that
    blends into a same-colored poster. `.poster-chip` instead gives the chip
    an opaque dark-scrim fill (see films.html.twig/series.html.twig's
    `.poster-chip` rule) and the is-success/is-danger modifier carries the
    status via colored text, which reads on both a poster and the flat
    detail-modal surface this partial also renders on.

    Params:
      present: list of { lang: string, hi: bool, forced: bool } — languages
               with subtitles already downloaded.
      missing: list of { lang: string, hi: bool, forced: bool } — languages
               still wanted.

    Renders nothing when both lists are empty.
#}
{% if present is not empty or missing is not empty %}
  <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-1">
    {% for c in present %}
      <span class="badge poster-chip is-success">{{ c.lang }}{% if c.hi %}<sup title="{{ 'bazarr.chips.hi_title'|trans }}">HI</sup>{% endif %}{% if c.forced %}<sup title="{{ 'bazarr.chips.forced_title'|trans }}">F</sup>{% endif %}</span>
    {% endfor %}
    {% for c in missing %}
      <span class="badge poster-chip is-danger">{{ c.lang }}{% if c.hi %}<sup title="{{ 'bazarr.chips.hi_title'|trans }}">HI</sup>{% endif %}{% if c.forced %}<sup title="{{ 'bazarr.chips.forced_title'|trans }}">F</sup>{% endif %}</span>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% endif %}
